    Configures the Windows installer: NSIS perMachine install, WebView2

    downloadBootstrapper (silent). Two integration tests guard the shape:

    tauri_conf_json_has_windows_bundle_block asserts the schema, and

    tauri_conf_json_no_unexpected_windows_keys gates against future schema drift.

    No macOS bundle key touched; bundle.targets stays 'all'.

    Note: the new test file is valid Rust but currently cannot be RUN because

    the devboule lib's #[cfg(test)] modules have 7 pre-existing compile errors

    (orphaned symbols after the ui-pilot removal: CommandBuilder, ps_single_quote,

    macos_codex_launch_line, MiniCoderBackendKind::Openai non-exhaustive, plus a

    few censor module references). Fixing those is a separate chore commit, not

    in scope for the Windows port. cargo build (without --tests) compiles clean.

